DEVIATIONS
Changes made by Hanzo AI, Inc. relative to upstream Casvisor:

- Rebranded the product to "Hanzo Visor": served web UI <title>
  (web/public/index.html) and README product name.
- Renamed the Go module github.com/casvisor/casvisor -> github.com/hanzoai/visor
  (go.mod); every casdoor/casvisor import was replaced with hanzoai/* — no
  casvisor or casdoor module remains in go.sum.
- Replaced the Casdoor authentication SDK with Hanzo IAM
  (github.com/hanzoai/iam) and Hanzo authz (github.com/hanzoai/authz);
  configuration reads iam* keys with a legacy casdoor* fallback
  (controllers/account.go).
- Added an in-process embed API — Bootstrap() and Handler()
  (pkg/visor/embed.go) — so the Hanzo cloud binary can mount Visor without a
  separate process.
- Added compute billing (billing/): fleet pricing at a flat one-third resell
  markup, with usage metering via github.com/hanzoai/commerce/metering
  (service/metering.go).
- Added analytics: emits compute fleet, cluster, and nodepool events into the
  analytics datastore (service/analytics.go, service/compute.go) with
  OpenTelemetry instrumentation (telemetry/).
- Routed object and machine storage through a pluggable storage seam (object/),
  backed by Hanzo Base.
- Added high-availability leader election via github.com/hanzoai/ha in the
  object coordinator (object/coordinator.go) and node autoscaling (autoscaler/).
- Default datastore is PostgreSQL (conf/app.conf: driverName=postgres, database
  hanzo_visor).
